**4.3 Data Usage Protocol**

All data are downloaded from their official repositories and processed exclusively within a secure computational environment. No protected health information is accessed, and no attempt at patient re‑identification is made. The FracEye‑Public release is accompanied by a Data Use Agreement that (i) restricts usage to non‑commercial research, (ii) prohibits re‑identification attempts, and (iii) requires citation of the original dataset publications. Any derived features are aggregated at a level that prevents inversion to original images.

